# Hetzner Deployment

**Council MCP runs on a Hetzner CCX23 VPS (16GB RAM, 4 vCPU) connected via Tailscale mesh.**

## SSH Access

Claude Code can SSH directly to the server:

```bash
ssh council-hub                    # Interactive shell
ssh council-hub "command"          # Run a command remotely
ssh council-hub "cd /opt/council_mcp && git pull"  # Pull latest code
```

**No password needed** — SSH keys are pre-configured over Tailscale. Use this for:
- Deploying changes (git pull + docker compose restart)
- Checking service health (`docker compose ps`)
- Viewing logs (`docker compose logs --tail 50 council-daemon`)
- Running backups
- Any server-side operation

## Directory Layout

**CRITICAL**: Dev PC and Hetzner have DIFFERENT directory structures. Never confuse them.

```
Dev PC (WSL2)                          Hetzner VPS (council-hub)
~/projects/MCP_SPINE/                  /opt/
├── council_mcp/                       ├── council_mcp/
├── scribe_mcp/                        ├── scribe_mcp/
├── corta_store/                       ├── corta_store/
└── ...                                └── backups/council/
```

- **Dev PC**: All repos under `~/projects/MCP_SPINE/` (parent dir is `MCP_SPINE`)
- **Hetzner**: All repos directly under `/opt/` (NO `MCP_SPINE` wrapper dir)
- **docker-compose.yaml** uses relative paths (`../../scribe_mcp`, `../../corta_store`) which resolve correctly from `council_mcp/deploy/` on BOTH layouts

**Tailscale hostname**: `council-hub`
**Secrets**: `/opt/council_mcp/secrets/*.txt` (chmod 600)
**Backups**: `/opt/backups/council/`

