## Docker Build Caching

The Dockerfile uses a two-layer pip install strategy:

1. **Layer 1** (cached): PyPI dependencies parsed from `pyproject.toml` (excluding agentkit). Cached until `pyproject.toml` changes.
2. **Layer 2** (rebuilt on code changes): Local packages — agentkit wheel from `vendor/` + council_mcp source.

This means code-only changes rebuild in ~5 seconds instead of re-downloading all packages.

